WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.960
In Kenya, a service called
M-Pesa lets people send

2
00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:06.040
and save money by phone.

3
00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:11.090
One study estimated that it
lifted about 194,000 households

4
00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:13.090
out of extreme poverty.

5
00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:16.590
That is about 2 per cent
of households in Kenya.

6
00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:19.930
Other countries cut tariffs,
sell state-owned firms,

7
00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:22.160
and invite foreign factories in.

8
00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:25.560
The idea is simple: let markets lead.

9
00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:28.370
So can opening up to
world markets and foreign

10
00:00:28.370 --> 00:00:30.930
firms make a poor country richer?

11
00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:33.800
In this mission, you'll
remove a tariff on a graph,

12
00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:36.300
and see who gains and who loses.

13
00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.810
Then you'll weigh up
small loans for people too

14
00:00:38.810 --> 00:00:40.860
poor for ordinary banks.

15
00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:44.930
Your mission: find out when
markets help a poor country grow.
